---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import waveImg from '../../../assets/posts/great-wave.jpg';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="The Great Wave off Kanagawa">
	<main>
		<nav><a href={base}>&larr; Home</a></nav>
		<h1>The Great Wave off Kanagawa</h1>
		<img class="post-image" src={waveImg.src} alt="The Great Wave off Kanagawa, woodblock print by Hokusai" />
		<figcaption>Katsushika Hokusai, c. 1831. Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons.</figcaption>
		<p>
			Katsushika Hokusai's woodblock print is the most recognizable work to come out
			of the ukiyo-e movement. It captures a moment of scale: three fishing boats
			dwarfed by a cresting wave, with Mount Fuji rendered small in the background.
		</p>
		<p>
			The composition's sense of vastness echoes a very different subject: see
			<a href={`${base}posts/earthrise/`}>Earthrise</a>, a photograph taken from
			lunar orbit that gave humanity its first view of Earth as a small, fragile
			whole.
		</p>
		<p>
			For a landscape captured on Earth rather than above it, see
			<a href={`${base}posts/grand-prismatic/`}>Grand Prismatic Spring</a>.
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
